### What is the Connect Level Order Siblings problem?

You are given a binary tree where each node has an extra `next` pointer (initially null). Connect each node to its immediate right neighbor on the same level. The last node on each level should have `next` pointing to null. After the operation, each level forms a singly linked list via the `next` pointers.

### How does the BFS solution work?

Use the standard level-size snapshot. Within each level, maintain a `previous` pointer that starts as null. For each dequeued node, if `previous` is not null, set `previous.next = node`. Then update `previous = node`. At the end of the level, the last node's `next` stays null.

```java
package com.bank.service;

import java.util.*;

public class SiblingConnector {

    static class TreeNode {
        int approverRank;
        TreeNode left, right, next;
        TreeNode(int val) { this.approverRank = val; }
    }

    public static void connectSiblings(TreeNode root) {
        if (root == null) return;

        Queue<TreeNode> queue = new LinkedList<>();
        queue.offer(root);

        while (!queue.isEmpty()) {
            int levelSize = queue.size();
            TreeNode previous = null;

            for (int i = 0; i < levelSize; i++) {
                TreeNode node = queue.poll();
                if (previous != null) {
                    previous.next = node;
                }
                previous = node;
                if (node.left != null) queue.offer(node.left);
                if (node.right != null) queue.offer(node.right);
            }
            // previous.next stays null (last node of level)
        }
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        TreeNode root = new TreeNode(1);
        root.left = new TreeNode(2);
        root.right = new TreeNode(3);
        root.left.left = new TreeNode(4);
        root.left.right = new TreeNode(5);
        root.right.right = new TreeNode(7);

        connectSiblings(root);

        // Print next pointers
        System.out.println("1.next = " + (root.next == null ? "null" : root.next.approverRank));
        System.out.println("2.next = " + root.left.next.approverRank);
        System.out.println("3.next = " + (root.right.next == null ? "null" : root.right.next.approverRank));
        System.out.println("4.next = " + root.left.left.next.approverRank);
        System.out.println("5.next = " + root.left.right.next.approverRank);
        System.out.println("7.next = " + (root.right.right.next == null ? "null" : root.right.right.next.approverRank));
    }
}
```

```text
